    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nPrivate detached residence with wonderful elevated sea views over Clogheen Strand towards Inchydoney Island, conveniently located only a 3km drive or 2km walk from Clonakilty town centre.\n\nThe property enjoys an exceptional elevated position overlooking the strand and surrounding countryside, with the south-facing aspect of the site ensuring natural light and sunshine throughout the day. The 0.86 acre (0.35ha) site includes a large area below the house with further potential for a variety of lifestyle uses.\n\nLocated on the Rocky Road, a quiet boreen which provides an idyllic 2 km. walk to Clonakilty town. The ancient highway once formed the primary route from Clonakilty to Castlefreke/Rathbarry and is first documented in the 17th century.\n\nFeatures include solar thermal panels for hotwater, oil fired central heating, double glazed windows, spacious reception areas, balcony terrace and a self-contained ground floor apartment providing additional accommodation potential for family, guests or home office use.\n\nThe main residence extends to approximately 168 sq.m. and the accommodation includes entrance hallway, spacious sitting room with large picture windows overlooking the estuary, kitchen/dining room with fitted units and access to the terrace, utility room, four bedrooms including master ensuite and family bathroom.\n\nThe lower ground floor incorporates a self-contained apartment comprising sitting room, kitchen area, bedroom and bathroom.\n\nThe property is approached by a driveway with mature hedging and planting providing a private sheltered setting. The elevated site enjoys views across Clogheen Strand and towards Inchydoney Island with surrounding gardens and terrace areas positioned to take full advantage of the coastal aspect.\n\nThe location is one of the property's most appealing features, positioned just a 5-minute drive approximately from Clonakilty town and within a safe 2km walk along the Rocky Road. Inchydoney Beach, local schools, sporting facilities and the many amenities of Clonakilty are all within easy reach making this an ideal permanent residence, holiday home or investment opportunity in one of West Cork's most sought-after coastal locations.\n\nDisclaimer:\nWhilst every care has been taken in the preparation of these particulars, all information is provided in good faith and is believed to be correct but is not guaranteed. Interested parties should satisfy themselves as to the accuracy and completeness of all details by independent inspection or enquiry. No representation or warranty is made regarding the condition, measurements, boundaries, planning status, services or other information relating to the property. All measurements, maps, photographs and distances are approximate and for guidance purposes only. Photographs, video and drone imagery are provided for illustrative purposes and may include features, furnishings or items not included in the sale."
      },
